n></li><li><span class="rf-year">494 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">Most Samian ships desert at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lade">Battle of Lade</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">440–439 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pericles">Pericles</a> crushes the Samian revolt</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">365 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> takes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samo">Samos</a> and settles it with Athenian cleruchs</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">129 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samo">Samos</a> becomes part of the Roman province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-roman-province">Asia</a></span></li></ol>
